# Root .dockerignore — applies to Docker builds whose context is the repo
# root, namely services/nb-bond-api/Dockerfile and services/nb-ui/Dockerfile.
# (services/blockscout/bens-microservice/Dockerfile uses its own subdirectory
# as build context, so it reads bens-microservice/.dockerignore instead.)
#
# Goal: send the minimum useful tar to the Docker daemon. Anything outside
# the two image-baked services' source trees + their npm-workspace metadata
# is excluded.

# Always-exclude
.git
.tmp
.codex
.claude
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.log
Handoff-AI-*.md
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local-only artefacts and secrets
.env
.env.*
contracts/.env
contracts/.env.example
services/nb-bond-api/helm/values.local.yaml
scripts/bid-submitter/examples/bids.keys.json

# Areas none of the image-baked services need in their build context
contracts
infra
docs
services/blockscout
services/script-runner

# Build / coverage / cache outputs (gitignored but worth re-excluding)
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/data
services/nb-bond-api/openapi.json

# Tests are not needed to produce either runtime image
services/nb-bond-api/tests
services/nb-ui/tests

# Editor / lint / format config files that don't affect the build output
**/.prettierrc
**/.prettierrc.json
**/.prettierignore
**/.gitignore
**/.dockerignore
**/eslint.config.mjs
**/babel.config.cjs
**/jest.config.cjs
**/tsconfig.test.json
**/AGENTS.md
**/DEVELOPMENT.md
**/README.md
